/-!
# Aux. lemma 57: the hydrodynamic derivative argument on an untouched interval

Packet PROVE-PRIMEEND (specification Aux. lemma 57, `source/spec/p241-288.md#aux-57`, pp. 254–256; used in Lemma
7.8's proof, p. 293: "Aux. lemma 57 fixes the argument lift on every untouched original-real interval and on the
transition from each ordinary single-prefix chart to the joint chart").

Let `A` be a compact `ℍ`-hull with mapping-out function `g` and canonical logarithm `L = log g′` (normalized at
`∞`, `Restart.IsCanonicalDerivLog`). If a real point `x` has a ball `B(x, ρ)` disjoint from `A`, then

  `L(z) → log g′(x) ∈ ℝ` as `z → x` in `ℍ`, in particular `Im L(z) → 0`   (HP1)

(`IsCanonicalDerivLog.tendsto_nhdsWithin_log`, `IsCanonicalDerivLog.tendsto_im_nhdsWithin_zero`): the derivative
argument has lift **zero**, not an unspecified multiple of `2π`.

## Proof (not the source's)

The source approximates `A` by finite unions of Jordan hulls generated by Loewner chains. We use instead the
**secant function** `S(z, w) = (ĝ(z) − ĝ(w))/(z − w)` (`= ĝ′(z)` on the diagonal), `ĝ` the Schwarz reflection of
`g` near the untouched real points. For a real `u` and `z ∈ ℍ` both `ĝ(z) − ĝ(u)` and `z − u` lie in `ℍ`, so
`S(z, u)` lies in the slit plane. Along a path `γ` from a real point `y` to a real point `x` through `ℍ \ A`, the
square lemma (`Aux57Square.exists_log_square`) applied to `(t, s) ↦ S(γ t, γ s)` (bottom edge `S(·, y)`, right edge
`S(x, ·)`, both in the slit plane) shows that the continuous logarithm of `g′ ∘ γ` changes by
`log ĝ′(x) − log ĝ′(y) ∈ ℝ`: the lift is the same integer at every untouched real point. At a real point `y` far to
the right, the vertical segment from `y` to a high point `p`, where `L = Log g′`, gives the integer `0`: there
`S(p, ·) ∈ B(1, 1/2)` (`|g − id| ≤ M`, `|g′ − 1| ≤ 1/4` high up).

## Main results

* `exists_isBdryReflection` : the Schwarz reflection `G` of `g` at an untouched real point is injective near it,
  with `G′(x) > 0` (open mapping theorem for the real points);
* `IsCanonicalDerivLog.exists_int_tendsto` : near an untouched real point `L = Log G′ + 2πin` (one integer `n`);
* `sub_eq_log_sub_log_of_path` : the path lemma (square lemma along a path between two real points);
* `IsCanonicalDerivLog.int_eq_of_two` (step 1), `IsCanonicalDerivLog.int_eq_zero_of_far` (step 2);
* `IsCanonicalDerivLog.tendsto_log_deriv`, `IsCanonicalDerivLog.tendsto_im_nhdsWithin_zero`,
  `IsCanonicalDerivLog.exists_tendsto_log` : (HP1);
* `IsCanonicalDerivLog.congr`, `IsCanonicalDerivLog.comp` : canonical logarithms see `g` only on `ℍ \ A`, and the
  chain rule `L_{g_C ∘ g_A} = L_C ∘ g_A + L_A` for `C = g_A(B \ A)`;
* `tendsto_im_sub_canonDerivLog` : Aux. 57 for chart transitions (`Im L_B − Im L_A → 0` where `g_A` tends to a real
  point untouched by the transition hull).

The `IsCanonicalDerivLog.*` theorems live in the namespace `InteractingSLE.Restart` (dot notation on
`Restart.IsCanonicalDerivLog`).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

open Complex Set Metric Filter Topology
open scoped Real ComplexConjugate

open SupercriticalConformalCovariance (IsConformalBijection)
open QuantumZipper (H Hbar)

